                "word": "schottische",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e3749c99-b0a9-4f42-a704-66f96ce56310",
                        "entry_id": "c32e841a-8f8b-376d-8b3e-26b2167fd576",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "schottisches"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e1827e0d-a3a2-3e5e-bae3-5aa555cede8e",
                        "entry_id": "c32e841a-8f8b-376d-8b3e-26b2167fd576",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A partnered country dance resembling a slow polka, probably of French origin, first introduced in England in 1848."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d428a7dc-d58b-40c3-b2ef-ecf39500b302",
                                "sense_id": "e1827e0d-a3a2-3e5e-bae3-5aa555cede8e",
                                "text": "The aim of whose existence appears to be that of rattling through the polka or schottische with the velocity of a spinning jenny."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1198ba35-2efc-41e3-b663-fb6329d90807",
                                "sense_id": "e1827e0d-a3a2-3e5e-bae3-5aa555cede8e",
                                "text": "[…] this abominable German usage we have imported—the polka and the schottish too […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44f07cef-2da3-4ea0-ac76-a8b7696b8a95",
                                "sense_id": "e1827e0d-a3a2-3e5e-bae3-5aa555cede8e",
                                "text": "[…] I could never dare to face Madame Mélanie Duval, or the Semiramis of dancing mistresses, Madame Michau Adelaide—study the fashionable steps in secret, and then burst upon the world as an adept in the Schottische, the Cellarius, and the Deux Temps?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9cf90b4d-ef05-49fe-abb6-2759868d7011",
                                "sense_id": "e1827e0d-a3a2-3e5e-bae3-5aa555cede8e",
                                "text": "The ‘Polka tremblante’, or Schottisch, is also a Bohemian national dance, and was brought out in Paris by Cellarius in 1844."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac5db574-8193-4d33-8d09-56ceae9ccea8",
                                "sense_id": "e1827e0d-a3a2-3e5e-bae3-5aa555cede8e",
                                "text": "[…] the Schottische is very seldom danced now in its original form[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6de5ca5-34c7-4bd6-be8e-e8a666010e7e",
                                "sense_id": "e1827e0d-a3a2-3e5e-bae3-5aa555cede8e",
                                "text": "It so happened that Pippi was learning to dance the shottische^([sic]), and she didn't want to go to bed until she was sure she could do it."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8f02df6e-6962-363d-bde1-8d5b8ae97b74",
                        "entry_id": "c32e841a-8f8b-376d-8b3e-26b2167fd576",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Music for the schottische."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce542974-fba9-4a2b-bbbe-dd5954ce3544",
                        "source_entry_id": "c32e841a-8f8b-376d-8b3e-26b2167fd576",
                        "source_sense_description": "a kind of dance",
                        "target_lang_word": "scottish",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scottish",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "907dab49-fa64-3c7a-a54a-f7c3f0c62e29",
                                        "entry_id": "c1ab69da-d62e-3861-b60d-f616744ed9c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Schottisch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4c17a5a-ded9-4588-a94e-8d6cdc14d31b",
                                                "sense_id": "907dab49-fa64-3c7a-a54a-f7c3f0c62e29",
                                                "text": "La scottish vous réclame, allons, messieurs, la main aux dames."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14a77b06-5bd6-4a84-801e-5e62f653d34b",
                                                "sense_id": "907dab49-fa64-3c7a-a54a-f7c3f0c62e29",
                                                "text": "Ce n’étaient que valses, mazurkas, polkas, pas-de-deux ou de–quatre, scottishs, dont chaque note avait sa verdeur, son entrain, sa grâce, son ingénuité que rehaussait le titre, allusion constante et délicate à nos paysages : Sur la route de Saint-Léger ; En revenant de Monlevade ; La barrière de Maindigour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "631177a0-f76d-4bd9-a3cf-1e46628156db",
                                                "sense_id": "907dab49-fa64-3c7a-a54a-f7c3f0c62e29",
                                                "text": "J’ai entendu tout ce que le jeune marié vient de dire à sa jeune mariée… Il lui a dit : « Encore une scottish et on leur brûle la politesse… »"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
